statement:
Let $n \geq 2$ be an integer, and let $a_1, a_2, \ldots, a_n$ be positive integers. Show that there exist positive integers $b_1, b_2, \ldots, b_n$ satisfying the following three conditions:
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(A)] $a_i \leq b_i$ for $i = 1, 2, \ldots, n$;
\item[(B)] the remainders of $b_1, b_2, \ldots, b_n$ on division by $n$ are pairwise different; and
\item[(C)] $b_1 + b_2 + \cdots + b_n \leq n\left(\dfrac{n-1}{2} + \left\lfloor\dfrac{a_1 + a_2 + \cdots + a_n}{n}\right\rfloor\right)$.
\end{enumerate}
